    "excerpt": "When an opening quote character indents the text block by 8 pixels, the eye registers an optical dent. CSS hanging-punctuation restores flawless vertical alignment.",
    "content": "\n      <p class=\"article-lead\">Gutenberg’s Bible of 1455 possessed an aesthetic subtlety that modern web browsers only recently mastered: hanging punctuation. By hanging hyphens and quotation marks into the outer margins, the solid rectangular texture of justified columns remained unbroken.</p>\n\n      <h2>The Mathematical Case for Optical Alignment</h2>\n      <p>When an opening double quotation mark sits inside the normal margin, the optical weight of the white space above the quotation mark creates an unsightly indentation. The eye perceives this as an accidental paragraph indent, breaking the reader’s left-edge tracking anchor.</p>\n\n      <pre><code class=\"language-css\">/* Modern CSS hanging punctuation standard */\n.article-prose {\n  hanging-punctuation: first allow-end;\n}</code></pre>\n\n      <h2>Micro-Typographic Flourishes</h2>\n      <p>True editorial elegance lives in the details: non-breaking thin spaces before em-dashes, tabular figures in financial columns, and discretionary ligatures in large display headlines.</p>\n    "
