    "excerpt": "Digital glass has always felt cold and slippery compared to heavy rag paper. By injecting fractional Brownian motion into fragment shaders, we give digital editorial typography physical weight.",
    "content": "\n      <p class=\"article-lead\">For centuries, the sensual pleasure of reading was inextricably bound to the physical fiber of the page: the textured tooth of 140lb cotton stock, the slight indentation where lead type struck dampened paper, and the subtle sheen of linseed ink.</p>\n\n      <h2>Procedural Paper Noise in Three Lines of GLSL</h2>\n      <pre><code class=\"language-glsl\">// GPU procedural paper tooth generation\nfloat paperNoise(vec2 uv) {\n  float n = fract(sin(dot(uv, vec2(12.9898, 78.233))) * 43758.5453);\n  return smoothstep(0.48, 0.52, n) * 0.035;\n}</code></pre>\n\n      <h2>Hardware-Accelerated Tactile Surfaces</h2>\n      <p>By delegating paper noise synthesis to the reader’s GPU via WebGL canvas overlays, CPU utilization remains below 2%, delivering smooth 60fps scrolling without taxing battery longevity.</p>\n    "
