    "content": "\n      <p class=\"article-lead\">For twelve years, responsive web development operated under a fundamental lie: that the width of the reader’s browser window determined how a component should render.</p>\n\n      <h2>The Component That Knows Itself</h2>\n      <pre><code class=\"language-css\">/* Native CSS Container Query pattern */\n.card-wrapper {\n  container-type: inline-size;\n}\n\n@container (min-width: 500px) {\n  .article-card {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 240px 1fr;\n    gap: 1.5rem;\n  }\n}</code></pre>\n\n      <h2>Spatial Modularity in Newsroom Design</h2>\n      <p>With container queries, authors and editors can drag any card into a narrow column, a panoramic banner, or a multi-tab drawer without breaking layout integrity.</p>\n    "
